cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Palimpsest data, feeds, or code in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Palimpsest: Censorship Observatory and Verifiable Eval Registry"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Palimpsest"
repository-code: "https://github.com/beepboop2025/palimpsest"
url: "https://palimpsest.info"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - censorship measurement
  - internet freedom
  - tamper-evident log
  - AI evaluation
  - transparency log
  - OSINT
  - China economy evidence
  - China money markets
  - CFETS
  - SHIBOR
  - Stock Connect
  - bitemporal economic data
  - Model Context Protocol
abstract: >-
  A public, tamper-evident record of what powerful actors quietly erase,
  verifiable offline by anyone, and a source-bound China Economic Observatory.
  Publishes aggregate CFETS money-market and HKEX Stock Connect evidence with
  separate economic-period, release and collection clocks, revisions, provenance,
  rights and explicit coverage abstentions. Seals AI evaluation results into an
  append-only registry (questions frozen before any model is queried, no
  edits after publication) and runs a live censorship observatory that
  treats deletion as data using open sources. Its public REST artifacts and
  read-only MCP tools preserve source and limitation context; they do not claim a
  validated economy-wide forecast or general capital-market coverage. Cite a
  specific signal and day via
  cite.html or scripts/build_citation_pack.py. Reproduce with
  python3 scripts/reproduce_all.py.
